WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.840
Hey this is Presh Talwalkar

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.320
Think of a two digit number

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.380
Add up the digits of the number together

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.020
Subtract your result from your original number

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.480
I want you to focus on this number

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.480
I'll call this your
magic number

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.900
In the following table locate your magic number

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.620
and concentrate on the symbol next to your number

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.420
If you have the number 4 for example

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.040
I want you to concentrate on the symbol of the person on the motorcycle.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.040
Are you concentrating on your symbol?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.440
Alright, I'm going to try and read your mind now.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
You're looking at the symbol of an eye.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.760
Did I get it correct?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.720
If you followed the directions correctly I did make the correct prediction.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.520
Why is this?

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.560
Let's go through the steps

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.900
A two digit number can be represented by a binomial 10 X plus y

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.880
When you add up the digits of the number that becomes the number X plus y

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.900
If you subtract the sum of the digits from the original number

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:22.400
the Y's will cancel out so you have 10 X minus X which is equal to 9 X

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.160
I don't know what your original
number is. I don't know what the sum of your digits are

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.300
but I know your magic
number will be a multiple of 9

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.120
In the table there will always be the same symbol for the multiples of 9 and that's the eye.

